I just ascended a 6 conduct monk, by the end of the game I had an AC
of -36, armorless.

I had an early lamp wish, but it went into a bag of holding. (soko was
"oR) I managed to survive to the castle wearing armor I found in
Ludios.

I literally dragged every single small shield, low boots, and high
boots I found in ludios to an altar. Took me three trips, but I got
out of it a +1 small shield and +4 low boots. Read an enchant armor
scroll on the shield and it came out +4.

By the castle, here was my armor:

+0 elven leather helm (chaotic, wasn't killing peaceful elves, didn't
want to wear a metal helmet)
+4 small shield
+2 leather gloves
+4 robe (read an enchant armor on the starting robe)
+4 low boots

With 9 points of divine protection, my ac was -18. That's plenty for
the castle. Got the wand, wished up some better armor, finished the
game at -36 AC, topped it off with another point of divine protection
and (lol) wished for a spellbook of drain life off the castle throne
to get everything to +5. That was overkill though and didn't have too
much use for the wish at that point with everything relevant genocided
and the castle wand still at 1:1.

+4 AC, though... gotta get the divine protection. Find Ludios.

